{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>התפול</b> — And behold, another parable: the birds of the sky, over which man has no dominion to fly and seize them — <b>התפול הצפור על פח</b> (shall a bird fall upon a trap) that is on the ground, <b>אם איננו למוקש</b> (if there is no snare for it)?! And behold, the meaning is that man, through his devices and cunning, can bring down the bird that is above him. And behold, I am above you and you are below, in my hand, and you have no wisdom against me. How will you escape the snare that I have decreed you be caught in? And the snare is the enemy that I will command to come upon you. And do not think that after it springs up it will be removed from you until vengeance is taken upon you. And this is <b>היעלה פח</b> (shall a trap spring up) — the meaning is: I will station it to besiege you."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:55.689939578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}